WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.250
- [Instructor] So let's
see how we could approach

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:07.150
four and 1/4 minus two and 2/4.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.050
Pause this video and have a go at that

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.783
before we work on this together.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:16.250
All right, so the first thing
that you might try to do

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:21.250
is re-write this as four
and 1/4 minus two and 2/4.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.460
And the reason why it's
useful to write it this way

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.870
is we could say look,
each of these mixed number

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:31.930
have a whole number part

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.610
and then they have a fractional part.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.740
And so I could try to
subtract the fractional part

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:36.670
from the fractional part

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.770
and then the whole number part
from the whole number part.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.930
And that will often work.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:42.790
But when we go to just
the fractional parts

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:46.120
and we say hey, how do
I subtract 2/4 from 1/4,

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.270
2/4 is larger than 1/4.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.290
You immediately might find yourself

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.260
in something of a conundrum.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.660
So what do you do?

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.760
Well, what comes to the rescue
is a notion called regrouping

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.520
and that's that we're not
just subtracting 2/4 from 1/4.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.200
We're subtracting two and
2/4 from four and 1/4.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.380
So what we could do is we
could take some of the value

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.000
that's in this four and
regroup it into the fraction.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.570
What do I mean by that?

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.900
Well instead of four,

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.900
if I view four as three and 4/4, 4/4.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:24.930
And so 4/4 plus 1/4 is 5/4, 5/4.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:29.090
So I could re-write this as three and 5/4

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.060
minus two and 2/4.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.750
Once again, why is that useful?

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.100
Because 5/4 is greater than 2/4.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.500
What is 5/4 minus 2/4?

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.570
Well that's going to be 3/4.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.220
And then what is three minus two?

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.630
Well that's going to be one.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:46.140
And we get one and 3/4.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.750
Another way we could of thought about it

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:52.523
is this is the same
thing as four minus two

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:58.713
plus 1/4, plus 1/4,

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:03.120
minus 2/4, minus 2/4.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.870
And we have trouble
with the 1/4 minus 2/4.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.570
That's what we saw right over here.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:10.320
So what we do is we take some
of that value from the four.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.320
Instead of four we could
re-write that as three plus 4/4.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.990
That's the same thing as four.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:23.990
And of course you have minus
two plus 1/4 minus 2/4.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.580
And then if you add the 4/4 to the 1/4

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.440
that's going to give us 5/4.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.200
So you're going to have three minus two.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.900
That's that part and that part.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.300
And then you're going to have

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.360
if you add the 4/4 and the 1/4,

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:42.200
so plus 5/4 minus 2/4.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.170
And that exactly what we have here.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:46.910
Three and 5/4, three and 5/4

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:52.810
minus two, minus two, and minus 2/4.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.080
And so three minus two is one.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:58.723
5/4 minus 2/4 is 3/4.

